Cryptographically generated base64 or base64url nonces are not directly affected because they do not contain HTML attribute delimiters. Exploitation requires an application to place attacker-controlled or otherwise unsafe data in `ssrContext.nonce`.

The remediation centralizes nonce handling across development SSR/SSG, production SSR, production SSG, critical CSS, store-state scripts, and Vue Devtools. It validates the value as a non-empty base64/base64url CSP nonce and HTML-encodes the attribute value before rendering.", "ghsa_id": "GHSA-5m6h-8g35-p3m7", "github_reviewed_at": "2026-10-07T16:16:03Z", "html_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5m6h-8g35-p3m7", "identifiers": [{"type": "GHSA", "value": "GHSA-5m6h-8g35-p3m7"}, {"type": "CVE", "value": "CVE-2026-106107"}], "nvd_published_at": "2026-10-06T18:16:52Z", "published_at": "2026-10-07T16:16:03Z", "references": ["https://github.com/quasarframework/quasar/security/advisories/GHSA-5m6h-8g35-p3m7", "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-106107", "https://github.com/quasarframework/quasar/commit/91271c38859bec51e154b60c24497a637ce903d7", "https://github.com/quasarframework/quasar/releases/tag/@quasar/app-vite-v3.3.0", "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5m6h-8g35-p3m7"], "repository_advisory_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/quasarframework/quasar/security-advisories/GHSA-5m6h-8g35-p3m7", "severity": "high", "source_code_location": "https://github.com/quasarframework/quasar", "summary": "Quasar Framework: App Vite SSR and SSG nonce attributes are not safely constrained", "type": "reviewed", "updated_at": "2026-10-07T16:16:03Z", "url": "https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-5m6h-8g35-p3m7", "vulnerabilities": [{"first_patched_version": "3.3.0", "package": {"ecosystem": "npm", "name": "@quasar/app-vite"}, "vulnerable_functions": [], "vulnerable_version_range": "<= 3.2.0"}], "withdrawn_at": null}
